# GitHub Workflow

Commits and branches: `git-workflow-and-versioning`. Issues, PRs, labels, assignees, reviews, merge: this rule. Before creating or editing an issue or PR, load `.cursor/skills/github-workflow/SKILL.md` — do not improvise `gh` flags.

## Linked bodies — tick before merge

Scope is the **PR body** plus every issue it names with `Closes` / `Fixes` / `Resolves` #N, open or closed. `- [ ]` and `* [ ]` are unfinished work: do the work, PATCH the body to `- [x]`, and never tick what you did not verify. After `gh pr merge` is too late.

Run this on the PR number and every linked issue number; if it prints anything, do not merge:

```bash
if gh api "repos/OWNER/REPO/issues/N" --jq .body | command grep -E '^[[:space:]]*[-*][[:space:]]+\[ \]'; then
  exit 1
fi
```

## Standard flow (mandatory on these use cases)

`issue → branch → PR with Closes #N → label + assignee → tick boxes → grep gate → review → green checks → merge`

Required when: the user asked for GitHub flow, an issue, or a PR; a bug has a durable repro; a feature needs acceptance criteria; work spans multiple PRs; other humans will review, or it is breaking / security / public behavior; it touches CI, install, or shared automation; an issue already covers it (`Closes #N`). Do not skip the flow to "avoid spam".

Do **not** open an issue for a one-file chore, a typo, or "so the PR has a number". Never invent `Closes`.

## Discover, don't invent

Read the repo before acting: `gh repo view --json nameWithOwner,defaultBranchRef`, `gh label list`, and the collaborator list. Never create labels. Never assign or request review from a login that is not a collaborator, and never from the PR author.

Exactly one type label if it exists: `bug` | `enhancement` | `chore` | `documentation`; ask if it is missing. `automated` only on bot/sync PRs.

## Assign, review, merge

- `--assignee "@me"` when the authenticated user is a collaborator; ask when other humans have push.
- Ask before a GitHub review when the diff is large or touches more than a few files.
- Solo: `gh pr review --comment`, never `--approve` on your own PR.
- Merge only when `gh pr checks` is green **and** the grep gate above prints nothing.
